{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 19,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.447,
            0.97,
            0.552,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.094,
            0.868,
            0.129
          ],
          "content": "Non-metals form negatively charged ions by gaining electrons when reacting with **metals.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.131,
            0.674,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": "Non-metals form oxides which are either acidic or neutral."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.151,
            0.868,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": "n **Non-metals do not displace hydrogen from dilute acids. They react with hydrogen to form hydrides.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.227,
            0.59,
            0.259
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "E X E R C I S E S"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.28,
            0.697,
            0.3
          ],
          "content": "**1. Which of the following pairs will give displacement reactions?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.302,
            0.492,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": "**(a) NaCl solution and copper metal**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.322,
            0.538,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "**(b)** $\\mathrm { M g C l } _ { 2 }$ **solution and aluminium metal**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.343,
            0.489,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": "**(c)** $\\mathrm { F e S O } _ { 4 }$ **solution and silver metal**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.363,
            0.507,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": "**(d)** $\\mathrm{AgNO_{3}}$ **solution and copper metal.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.382,
            0.87,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": "**2. Which of the following methods is suitable for preventing an iron frying pan from rusting?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.42,
            0.355,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": "**(a) Applying grease**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.44,
            0.347,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Applying paint**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.46,
            0.439,
            0.48
          ],
          "content": "**(c) Applying a coating of zinc**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.48,
            0.35,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": "**(d) All of the above.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.5,
            0.871,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": "**3. An element reacts with oxygen to give a compound with a high melting point. This compound is also soluble in water. The element is likely to be**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.538,
            0.284,
            0.557
          ],
          "content": "**(a) calcium**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.557,
            0.278,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": "**(b) carbon**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.577,
            0.273,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": "**(c) silicon**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.598,
            0.254,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": "**(d) iron.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.618,
            0.655,
            0.636
          ],
          "content": "**4. Food cans are coated with tin and not with zinc because**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.638,
            0.414,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": "**(a) zinc is costlier than tin.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.657,
            0.559,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": "**(b) zinc has a higher melting point than tin.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.678,
            0.467,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": "**(c) zinc is more reactive than tin.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.698,
            0.456,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": "**(d) zinc is less reactive than tin.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.717,
            0.707,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": "**5. You are given a hammer, a battery, a bulb, wires and a switch.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.737,
            0.87,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "**(a) How could you use them to distinguish between samples of metals and non-metals?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.772,
            0.869,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Assess the usefulness of these tests in distinguishing between metals and non-metals.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.808,
            0.777,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "**6. What are amphoteric oxides? Give two examples of amphoteric oxides.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.828,
            0.87,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "**7. Name two metals which will displace hydrogen from dilute acids, and two metals which will not.**"
        },
